<p class="note">A month with no posts breaks the orange line rather than touching the
floor. A logarithmic axis has no position for zero, and drawing it at the bottom would read
as <em>very little</em> when it means <em>none</em>. <strong>Two different absences sit on
this chart and they are marked differently.</strong> 2025-09 is a measured zero - the export
covers that month and it contains no posts - and is labelled <em>0 posts</em> at the axis.
2026-07 is not a measurement at all: the Medium index was exported 2026-07-07 and cannot
contain anything published after that date, so the boundary is drawn as a rule in the
published series' own colour. Nothing is plotted as a point in either case.</p>

