        <h2 id="evidence-title" class="visually-hidden">Evidence and boundary</h2>

        <details class="disclosure">
          <summary>Evidence and boundary for this reading</summary>

          <div class="disclosure-body">
            <p>
              This page presents one measurement of a working corpus, bounded at
              31 July 2026, 23:59:59, Asia/Taipei. Unlike the slice of 25 July
              2026, that date is a cut-off and not an observation: nothing dated
              after it was counted, and the counting itself happened later. A
              later assembly time does not move the boundary.
            </p>
            <p>
              The corpus measured is a private working corpus. What is public is
              the result: the two data files committed in the source
              repository and pinned below. The corpus itself is not published, and this page is
              not a route into it.
            </p>
            <p>
              The charts are pre-rendered from those two files. Nothing is
              computed when the page is viewed, so the drawing cannot drift from
              the figures it pins.
            </p>
            <p>
              The measurements are ordered. The order does not explain them.
              Nothing below establishes that any one of these states caused
              another.
            </p>

            <dl class="evidence-list">
              {
                MEASUREMENTS.map((measurement) => (
                  <div class="evidence-entry">
                    <dt>{measurement.phrase}</dt>
                    <dd>
                      <p class="observed">{measurement.observedFact}</p>
                      <p class="pinned">
                        <span class="pinned-label">Committed</span>
                        {" "}
                        {measurement.evidence.timestamp}
                        <br />
                        <span class="pinned-label">Commit</span>
                        {" "}
                        <span class="sha">{measurement.evidence.sha}</span>
                      </p>
                      <p class="traverse">
                        <span class="pinned-label">Files</span>
                        {
                          measurement.evidence.paths.map((entry) => (
                            <>
                              {" "}
                              <a href={entry.url}>{entry.path}</a>
                            </>
                          ))
                        }
                      </p>
                      <p class="limit">{measurement.boundary}</p>
                    </dd>
                  </div>
                ))
              }
            </dl>

            <p class="disclosure-close">
              Each reference is pinned to a fixed commit. That these figures can
              be checked does not establish that they are true of the corpus;
              this page asks to be believed no further than the files show.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
